:0.9,"location":{"file":"CHANGELOG.md","start_line":1,"end_line":18},"finding":null,"explanation":"This file’s natural-language content is fully Chinese, including the title and all update notes, with no indication that users may choose another language. Under the policy rule, forcing a specific language without opt-in can be a natural-language policy concern unless the locale restriction is explicitly justified.","remediation":"Add a note that the skill documentation is localized for Chinese users, provide multilingual alternatives, or explicitly state that language selection is user-configurable or region-specific.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"CHANGELOG.md","start_line":1,"end_line":18}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-f588c617811249b5b030f06406ba155a","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"README.md","start_line":5,"end_line":6},"finding":null,"explanation":"The README states that the skill is 'for Chinese creators' in both Chinese and English, which presents a locale-targeting constraint in natural language. Because the file does not clarify that this is an optional audience focus or provide an explicit language/locale choice, it can be interpreted as a policy-relevant locale restriction.","remediation":"Clarify that the skill can be used in multiple languages/locales, or explicitly state that the Chinese focus is optional and based on the Douyin use case. If the locale restriction is intentional, document the justification clearly.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"README.md","start_line":5,"end_line":6}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-1cfb98d0ba4342039d5740101ab4b6aa","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"docs/USAGE.md","start_line":1,"end_line":25},"finding":null,"explanat